# CRM ↔ OpenHouse Core — Staging API Guide

This document describes how the **CRM system** should integrate with the **two new server-to-server APIs** deployed on **staging**.

---

## Environment

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| **Base URL** | `https://staging-561394753846.asia-south2.run.app/api/v1/oh/` |
| **Auth header** | `X-CRM-Key: <CRM_API_KEY>` |
| **Content-Type** | `application/json` |

The staging `CRM_API_KEY` has been shared separately via **personal DM** — do not commit it to code or docs.

Both APIs use the **same `X-CRM-Key`** already configured for CRM server-to-server calls on staging. **No separate API key is required.**

---

## Authentication

Every request must include:

```http
X-CRM-Key: <CRM_API_KEY>
```

| HTTP status | Meaning |
|-------------|---------|
| `401 Unauthorized` | Missing or invalid key |
| `503 Service Unavailable` | `CRM_API_KEY` not configured on the server |

---

## New APIs at a glance

| # | Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|--------|----------|---------|
| 1 | `PUT` | `/schedule-visits/{visit_id}/` | Complete or cancel a visit from CRM |
| 2 | `GET` | `/crm/home-sales-manager/?home_id=` | Get sales manager assigned to a home |
| 2 | `POST` | `/crm/home-sales-manager/` | Assign, update, or unassign home sales manager |

For visit completion, CRM must already have the OpenHouse **`visit_id`** (from your system’s stored mapping).

