## Implementation checklist for CRM team

- [ ] Store `CRM_API_KEY` securely (env / secrets manager) — value received via **personal DM**
- [ ] Implement **Home SM** GET/POST if CRM owns home–SM mapping
- [ ] Persist OpenHouse **visit `id`** in CRM for completion/cancel calls
- [ ] On complete: choose **OTP** vs **Assisted** payload based on your UI flow
- [ ] Always send `selected_date` + `selected_time` on visit update
- [ ] Verify `platform: "crm"` in the response after complete/cancel
- [ ] Handle `401` / `404` / `422` as documented above

---

## Notes

- **No app release required** for these CRM APIs — they are server-to-server only.
- The mobile app continues to use session auth on the same visit update URL; CRM and app paths are independent.
- Request JSON may use **snake_case**; responses may use **camelCase** depending on the API renderer.

---

## CRM API key

The staging **`CRM_API_KEY`** has been sent in a **personal DM**. Use that value in the `X-CRM-Key` header for all requests above.
